    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "could u be more specific about the raas cycle though? like what happens to the aldosterone levels and the renin when the ACE is inhibited? i'm trying to get the full sequence down.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When ACE is inhibited, the production of Angiotensin II decreases, which in turn reduces the stimulation of aldosterone release from the adrenal glands. Lower aldosterone levels mean less sodium and water retention by the kidneys, contributing to lower blood volume and thus lower blood pressure. Additionally, the decreased Angiotensin II signaling can sometimes affect the renin release, although the primary action is the downstream reduction in vasoconstriction and aldosterone effects.",
      "source": "target",
